{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"0db4c438-74ec-4bb8-a1fc-724adbd5d013","title":"Chance a dart lands in a circle inside a square"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0db4c438-74ec-4bb8-a1fc-724adbd5d013","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Suppose a dart lands uniformly at random inside this square. The circle fits exactly inside, touching all four sides.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Probability from area"},{"op":"figure","id":"target","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1.4,1.4],"y":[-1.4,1.4],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"square","points":[[-1,-1],[1,-1],[1,1],[-1,1]],"closed":true},{"kind":"circle","id":"circle","center":[0,0],"r":1}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0db4c438-74ec-4bb8-a1fc-724adbd5d013","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Shade the successful landing region. With uniform landing, probability equals the shaded area divided by the entire square's area.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"shade","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"shade","inside":"circle"},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[1,0],"label":"r"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"ratio","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\text{circle})=\\frac{\\text{area of circle}}{\\text{area of square}}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0db4c438-74ec-4bb8-a1fc-724adbd5d013","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The radius is r, so the square's side is twice r. What areas belong in our probability ratio?","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"side","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[-1,-1.16],"to":[1,-1.16],"label":"2r"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"areas","anchor":{"el":"ratio","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"A_{\\text{circle}}=\\pi r^2,\\qquad A_{\\text{square}}=(2r)^2=4r^2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What ratio gives the probability of landing inside the circle?","expected_gist":"Divide pi r squared by 4r squared."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0db4c438-74ec-4bb8-a1fc-724adbd5d013","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The radius cancels. About 78.5 percent of uniformly landing darts hit the circle, regardless of the target's size.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"areas","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P=\\frac{\\pi r^2}{4r^2}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\approx 0.785=78.5\\%"},{"op":"figure","id":"finish","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.48],"text":"78.5%","size":"large"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
